            <ArticleTitle>Protecting the back during pregnancy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>286-91</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Although pregnancy is a healthy condition, anatomical changes do occur that cause poor alignment and low back pain. A pregnant worker will feel stronger and more comfortable if she maintains her pelvis in a tilted position. The occupational health nurse can instruct the pregnant worker about exercises and proper body mechanics so that she maintains good spine alignment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
